  "body": "## What changed\n\nPR #2157 corrected the frame basis for new tilts. A tilt that loads from a file without `basis_version` keeps the legacy basis 0. The operation page and MCP `edit_operation` kept basis 0 when the user set new angles on such a tilt. At A0/B180, the basis-0 frame turns plane X to world Y. The same slot then posts XY that is turned 90 degrees.\n\n- `EditOperationParams` now calls `OpParams::with_stepped_tilt_basis` (new file `crates/app/src/operation/types/tilt_basis.rs`).\n- When an edit changes the A or B angle of a basis-0 tilt, the tilt gets basis 1 (`CURRENT_TILT_BASIS`).\n- An edit that keeps the angles (origin, feed, depth) keeps basis 0.\n- An old file that the user does not edit posts the same program as before (`tilt_basis_compat`, `first_4axis_part`).\n- Undo restores the legacy tilt with basis 0.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2599-a180-legacy-basis.md`.\n\n## Routes and results (Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, slot (10,0) -> (30,0), mm)\n\n| Route | Before the fix | After the fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| New operation at A0, A90, A-90, A0/B180 (basis 1) | correct XY | correct XY |\n| Old file, tilt not edited | posts its saved program (basis 0, deliberate) | same |\n| Old file, edit that keeps the angles | basis 0, same program | same |\n| Old file A90, angles set to A0/B180 on the operation page (`EditOperationParams`) | **turned 90 degrees**: `G1 X0 Y-10` -> `X0 Y-30` | `G1 X10 Y0` -> `X30 Y0` |\n| Old file A-90, MCP `edit_operation` with patch `{tilt:{a_deg:0,b_deg:180}}`, save, reopen | **turned 90 degrees**: `G1 X0 Y-10` -> `X0 Y-30` | `G1 X10 Y0` -> `X30 Y0` |\n| `tilt {a_deg:180}` refusal names A0/B180 | pinned by the existing `tilt_a180::out_of_range_tilt_refuses_by_name_with_a0_b180_remedy` | unchanged |\n\nI took the pre-fix readings with the new call disabled and the basis asserts commented out. Both legacy edit tests failed with `left: [(\"0\", \"-10\"), (\"0\", \"-30\")]`, `right: [(\"10\", \"0\"), (\"30\", \"0\")]`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `tilt_a180_routes::a0_a90_a_minus_90_and_a0_b180_post_the_same_local_xy`\n- `tilt_a180_routes::a_legacy_tilt_edited_to_a0_b180_on_the_operation_page_posts_the_same_local_xy`\n- `tilt_a180_routes::a_legacy_tilt_edited_to_a0_b180_over_mcp_posts_the_same_local_xy`\n- `tilt_a180_routes::a_legacy_tilt_keeps_its_basis_when_its_angles_do_not_change`\n- lib `operation::types::tilt_basis::tests::new_angles_step_a_legacy_basis_and_kept_angles_do_not`\n- lib `operation::types::tilt_basis::tests::the_tilt_slot_covers_each_kind_whose_file_shape_has_a_tilt`\n\nRegression runs: `tilt_a180` (2), `tilt_basis_compat` (7) and `first_4axis_part` (4) all pass.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head 397951da0: 23 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not started. The operation-page route is tested through `EditOperationParams` with the loaded tilt edited in place, which is what the page does.\n- The CLI and script routes were not run. A search found no tilt writer in them other than the JSON door (basis 1) and `EditOperationParams`.\n- A copy of a legacy operation keeps basis 0 on purpose, so that it cuts like its source. An edit of its angles then steps the basis.\n- Only an A-only machine (microARC 4) was used. No AC or BC trunnion was used.\n\nChangelog: A 3+2 operation from an older project that is set to new tilt angles (for example A0/B180) now posts its plane XY like a new operation, not turned 90 degrees.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2599\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
